Request

Give me a carefully researched and structured development plan for building the following application. Do not rush into implementation. I want to micro-plan the project first and then build it step by step.

Product concept

I want to build a Quran reading and recitation assistance app, tentatively called “Ustad” or something similar.

The app should work like a combination of a Quran teacher and karaoke-style recitation interface:

* The user sees the Quran on screen.
* As the user recites, the app should follow their recitation in real time.
* The word currently being recited should be highlighted/traced.
* If the user recites a word incorrectly, the app should identify and highlight the error.
* It should detect:
    * Incorrect words
    * Incorrect pronunciation
    * Skipped words
    * Extra words
    * Words recited out of sequence
* The UI should clearly show where the user is in the Ayah.
* The experience should feel natural and responsive, similar to karaoke, but function like a Quranic teacher.

Critical technical challenge

I have attempted to build something similar before.

My biggest problems were:

1. Recitation tracking was unreliable — the highlighted word would not follow the user’s actual recitation correctly.
2. False positives/false errors — the system would incorrectly mark correct recitation as wrong.
3. Repeated words or Ayahs — when the same word or phrase appears multiple times, the system could lose track of where the user actually is.

These are the most important problems to solve.

The system should only track the Quranic words that are currently visible/on screen.

If a word, phrase, or Ayah appears multiple times, the system must not assume which occurrence the user is reciting until there is sufficient confidence from the audio/alignment/context.

Accuracy and robust alignment are more important than simply making the application appear to work.

Audio and Quran requirements

The target audience is primarily India and Pakistan, so choose the appropriate:

* Arabic Quran script
* Quran text source
* Unicode representation
* Diacritics handling
* Arabic normalization strategy
* Speech/audio processing approach
* ASR model
* Pronunciation/alignment model

The system must preserve the Quranic text accurately and should not modify the displayed Quran text merely to make speech recognition easier.

I also want a feature where the user can tap/click the marker at the end of an Ayah and listen to that Ayah being recited by a professional Qari.

The professional recitation should be synchronized with the displayed Ayah.

Technology requirements

I have an Intel-based Mac.

I have very limited/no technical knowledge, so the entire development workflow needs to be designed around this constraint.

Whenever possible:

* Automate setup.
* Automate installation.
* Automate configuration.
* Provide scripts that I can run by double-clicking files.
* Avoid requiring me to manually execute complicated terminal commands.
* Make development, testing, deployment, and troubleshooting as automated as reasonably possible.

I want the project pushed to Git.

I want to host the application privately online so that I can access and test it from mobile devices.

The final product should primarily be designed for mobile users.

Models and APIs

Use open-source models wherever practical.

If an external API is genuinely necessary, tell me:

* Which API is required
* Why it is required
* Estimated cost
* Whether there is a free/cheap alternative
* Whether it introduces privacy or latency concerns
* Whether it can eventually be replaced with an open-source model

Keep the project economical and cost-effective.

Do not choose an expensive model simply because it is easier to integrate.

Architecture

I want you to carefully evaluate the best architecture for:

* Mobile UI
* Quran rendering
* Microphone/audio capture
* Audio streaming
* Voice activity detection
* ASR
* Forced alignment / phoneme alignment
* Word-level alignment
* Pronunciation evaluation
* Error detection
* Recitation tracking
* Handling skipped/extra/repeated words
* Confidence scoring
* Real-time feedback
* Professional Qari playback
* Backend processing
* Database/storage
* Authentication if required
* Private hosting
* Logging and debugging

Pay particular attention to latency and real-time word tracking.

Do not use browser-side speech recognition if a better architecture is available. Evaluate whether audio should be captured in the browser/mobile client and streamed to the backend for processing.

Accuracy requirements

The application should not aggressively mark a user as wrong when the system is uncertain.

I would prefer a system that says “uncertain — continue listening” rather than incorrectly marking a correct recitation as wrong.

Design a confidence-based system where appropriate.

The system should distinguish between:

* Definitely correct
* Probably correct
* Uncertain
* Probably incorrect
* Definitely incorrect

Research the best technical approach for Quran recitation specifically rather than assuming that a generic speech-to-text pipeline will be sufficient.

Consider whether a combination of ASR + forced alignment + phoneme-level analysis + Quran-specific rules would provide better results than relying on a single LLM or ASR model.

Development methodology

Do not immediately start coding.

First:

1. Understand the complete product requirements.
2. Research the available open-source models and datasets.
3. Compare the viable technical architectures.
4. Identify the hardest technical problems.
5. Determine what should be proven with a prototype before building the full application.
6. Identify risks and likely failure points.
7. Select versions of frameworks, libraries, models, and runtimes that are appropriate for my Intel Mac and eventual deployment environment.
8. Create a phased implementation plan.
9. Define clear acceptance criteria for each phase.
10. Only then begin implementation.

I want the project micro-planned, but do not get lost in unnecessary micro-planning.

The goal is to build the best practical version, not endlessly plan.

At every major decision point, if there are multiple technically reasonable options, research them first and then ask for my opinion before committing.

If you need information from me, ask specific questions rather than making assumptions.

Important constraints

* Do not invent APIs, Quran data sources, models, or libraries.
* Do not blindly follow a popular architecture if it is unsuitable for this application.
* Do not over-engineer unnecessarily.
* Do not prioritize speed of development over recitation accuracy.
* Do not use an LLM as a substitute for deterministic audio alignment where a specialized audio model/algorithm would be more appropriate.
* Do not assume that normal Arabic ASR accuracy is sufficient for Quran recitation evaluation.
* Treat repeated words, repeated phrases, and similar Ayahs as a major alignment problem.
* Only evaluate/track the Quran text that is currently visible to the user.
* Preserve the exact Quranic text and ordering.
* Design the system so that individual components can later be replaced with better models.

